Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

•
Triage, validate, and prioritize security findings from SAST, SCA, and Secret scanning tools, filter out false positives, assess risks, and track issues through to remediation;

•
Conduct manual and tool-assisted code reviews to identify security vulnerabilities, logic flaws, and insecure implementation choices before code reaches production;

•
Perform hands-on penetration testing of web applications, microservices, and APIs to uncover security vulnerabilities and business logic flaws;&nbsp;

•
Audit REST and GraphQL APIs and web applications with a strong focus on core application security risks, authentication, authorization, and business logic.

We need your professional experience:

•
2-4 years of experience in Application Security, Product Security, or Penetration Testing;&nbsp;

•
Hands-on experience triaging and analyzing findings from Semgrep / OpenGrep, Gitleaks, Trivy, and OSV-Scanner;

•
Experience with Burp Suite (Pro), Nuclei, Subfinder, SQLmap, Metasploit, and NetExec;&nbsp;

•
Deep understanding of classic OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities, including Injection flaws (SQLi, Command Injection), Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF), Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF), Broken Access Control / Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR / BOLA), Security Misconfigurations, Cryptographic Failures, Insecure Deserialization, and Mass Assignment;

•
Solid knowledge of OWASP API Security Top 10 for REST and GraphQL architectures;&nbsp;

•
Deep understanding of identity protocols and access control mechanics (OAuth 2.0, OIDC, JWT, SAML, RBAC/ABAC);

•
Ability to identify complex authorization bypasses, session management flaws, and business logic bugs;

•
Ability to read and analyze modern application code to spot security flaws (will be a plus);&nbsp;

•
Understanding of cloud security principles in AWS environments and Kubernetes (K8s) security fundamentals (will be a plus);

•
Intermediate level of English (spoken and written).

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

•
Strong communication skills to effectively collaborate with engineering, product, and DevOps teams;

•
Result-oriented mindset;

•
Openness to learning.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

•
GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

•
DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

•
BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.

Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

•
Lead the VIP brand strategy for the LATAM region, setting the tone of voice, positioning, and overall creative direction;

•
Build impactful and localized brand experiences, from gifting to communications, that reflect user preferences, cultural nuances, and seasonal trends;

•
Collaborate closely with the VIP Event Manager to craft exclusive, personalized event concepts that surprise and delight VIP users;

•
Work alongside CRM, design, and social media teams to ensure a cohesive and compelling brand presence across all customer touchpoints;

•
Propose and execute influencer and ambassador partnerships tailored to key LATAM markets;

•
Monitor and analyze market trends, competitor activity, and shifting user behavior to inform strategy and refine initiatives;

•
Deliver post-campaign reports and event recaps with performance metrics, user insights, and future recommendations;

•
Maintain brand quality and consistency across all activations, from visual assets to gifting execution and user communications;

•
Coordinate with legal, procurement, finance, and external agencies to ensure smooth and timely project delivery.

We need your professional experience:

•
Experience in Brand Marketing, Brand Management, or VIP Marketing, preferably within the iGaming or entertainment sectors;

•
A deep understanding of LATAM markets;

•
Proven success in developing and launching creative campaigns or VIP-focused brand experiences;

•
Strong project management and cross-functional collaboration skills;

•
Comfort working with performance metrics, budgets, and light Excel reporting;

•
Advanced English proficiency and/or Portuguese fluency.

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

•
Strategic thinker with a pulse on branding, customer psychology, and cultural relevance in LATAM;

•
Creative, resourceful, and confident in pitching and pushing new ideas;

•
Organized and detail-oriented, able to see projects through from concept to execution;

•
Proactive and independent, you take ownership and move ideas forward without waiting for direction;

•
Highly collaborative, you thrive working across departments and geographies;

•
Comfortable managing KPIs, timelines, and budgets in a fast-paced environment.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

•
GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

•
DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

•
BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.

Se você tem paixão por inovação e busca trabalhar em um ambiente que promove agilidade, colaboração e desafiados, esta pode ser a sua oportunidade!
Para nosso time de Engenharia , buscamos pessoas talentosas e capazes de construir sistemas complexos e de alta qualidade.
Você estará diretamente envolvido com o negócio através da construção e manutenção de nossos sistemas. Nosso principal pilar é a qualidade daquilo que entregamos, entendemos que o importante é fazer bem feito ao invés de fazer rápido. Focamos na simplicidade da solução, nas entregas em pequenas partes e na autonomia das pessoas desenvolvedoras, a partir de um trabalho colaborativo.
Como o nosso ecossistema está em constante evolução, esta oportunidade é focada em um de nossos produtos de ponta em Inteligência Artificial. Por isso, embora a maior parte do ecossistema Asaas utilize Java, esta estrutura é construída em .NET .
Buscamos profissionais com sólida base em engenharia de software, paixão por arquitetura moderna, autonomia para navegar em cenários ambíguos e total abertura para o ecossistema de agentes de IA!
Se interessou pela oportunidade mas não reside em Joinville? Não tem problema, possibilitamos o trabalho remoto/home office .

• Transformar lógica de negócio em código de alta qualidade, defendendo a simplicidade e as boas práticas de arquitetura;

• Participar ativamente da arquitetura, definição e implementação de novas funcionalidades, além da correção de bugs;

• Compreender problemas complexos com pouca definição inicial e estruturar soluções técnicas robustas;

• Revisar o código entregue pelos colegas de equipe, atuando como um facilitador e elevando a maturidade técnica do time;

• Dividir grandes entregas em pequenos entregáveis coesos e de valor contínuo;

• Monitorar a estabilidade, performance e o comportamento da solução implementada em produção;

• Colaborar ativamente com melhorias, documentação e novos padrões na base de conhecimento da Engenharia.

• Sólida experiência com o ecossistema .NET;

• Experiência com desenvolvimento Web;

• Experiência na construção e consumo de APIs REST;

• Vivência prática com bancos de dados relacionais (preferencialmente PostgreSQL);

• Domínio de versionamento com Git e noções de pipeline de CI/CD;

• Inglês técnico.

Informações adicionais
Diferenciais

• Conhecimento ou vivência com o ecossistema Angular;

• Vivência com Inteligência Artificial (desenvolvimento de Agentes de IA, lógicas de automação ou uso de LLMs);

• Experiência com integrações de WhatsApp API;

• Noções de monitoramento de aplicações em produção (logs, performance e telemetria).

Modelo de trabalho

• Carga horária de 8h por dia (segunda à sexta-feira - não compensamos os sábados);

• Contratação CLT.

